-- title:
--   Penalty bounds for regions 0 to 15 of level-three band 5
-- statement:
--   A bound on the rational Gibbs-dual penalty expression for regions 0 to 15 of
--   level-three band 5.
--
--   Each region carries a reference attached to every split of its parent shape, built as a product of
--   small primes with integer exponents. The bound says that for each of these regions the resulting
--   rational expression -- the total reference mass over all splits, minus two, plus the sum of the
--   squared split weights divided by their references -- stays below an explicit rational with
--   denominator ten to the thirtieth.
-- source:
--   Duan-Wu-Zhou fourth-power recursive construction (https://arxiv.org/html/2210.10173v5, section 7) combined with the More-Asymmetry regional extraction (https://arxiv.org/html/2404.16349v2, section 6). Exact finite or asymptotic-rate statement as written; no exponent claim.

